<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='en-US'><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><script>window['ec:pageId']='10132456548248554955'</script><title>CFP</title><link href="/images/favicon.ico" rel="icon" type="image/jpeg"/><link href="/css/cool.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<link href="/css/cfp/classic.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<link href="/css/menu_cfp.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<script src="/js/easy.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/menu.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/form.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/inplace.js?version=545"></script><script>EC.version='545'</script></head>
<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">AICAS 2027: The 9th IEEE International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Circuits and Systems</div><div id="cfpvenue"></div><div id="cfpdateplace">Hangzhou, China, September 20-22, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/" target="_blank">https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=aicas2027" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=aicas2027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>April 13, 2027</td></tr></table><p>The 9<sup>th</sup> IEEE International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Circuits and Systems (AICAS 2027) will be held in Hangzhou, China during September 20-22, 2027.</p><p>The next generation of AI will not only answer: it will perceive, plan and act, in robots, vehicles, wearables and autonomous agents. AICAS 2027 invites contributions on the circuits and systems that make this possible, under tight limits of energy, latency, memory and safety.</p><p>AICAS 2027 aims to offer an excellent platform allowing world scholars, technology researchers, and industry to exchange experiences, demonstrate their studies, and further advance AI circuits and systems technologies.</p><h2>Organizing Committee</h2><h3>General Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Amara Amara</strong>, Beihang University, China</li></ul><h3>General Co-Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Weisheng Zhao</strong>, Beihang University, China</li></ul><h3>Technical Program Committee Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Yoshifumi Nishio</strong>, Tokushima University, Japan</li></ul><h3>Technical Program Committee Co-Chairs</h3><ul><li><strong>Xueyan Wang</strong>, Beihang University, China</li><li><strong>Zhou Jin</strong>, Hong Kong University, China</li></ul><h3>Special Sessions Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Hanhoo Lee</strong>, Inha University, South Korea</li></ul><h3>Special Sessions Co-Chairs</h3><ul><li><strong>Xiaotao Jia</strong>, Beihang University, China</li><li><strong>Antoine Frappe</strong>, Lille University, France</li></ul><h3>Tutorial Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Yen-Kuang Chen</strong>, Intel, USA</li></ul><h3>Tutorial Co-Chairs</h3><ul><li><strong>Mohamad Sawan</strong>, Westlake University, China</li><li><strong>Yen-Kuang Chen</strong>, University of Tennessee, USA</li></ul><h3>Publicity Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Wei Mao</strong>, Southern University of Science and Technology, China</li></ul><h3>Finance Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Ge Tong</strong>, NTU, Singapore</li></ul><h3>Finance Co-Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Amara Amara</strong>, Beihang University, China</li></ul><h3>Industry Liaison Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Victor Grimblatt</strong>, Synopsys, Chile</li></ul><h3>Industry Liaison Co-Chairs</h3><ul><li><strong>Preet Yadav</strong>, NXP Semiconductors, India</li><li><strong>Wenzhuo Zhang</strong>, Alibaba Hangzhou, China</li><li><strong>Eimer Sylvain</strong>, Truth Equipment, Ltd, China</li></ul><h3>Local Arrangement Chair</h3><ul><li><strong>Yueting Li</strong>, Beihang University, China</li></ul><h3>Conference Assistant</h3><ul><li><strong>Zou Xi</strong>, Zhejiang International Studies University, China</li></ul><h2>List of Topics</h2><ul><li>Hardware for embodied AI: perception, sensor fusion, motion control and robotics processors</li><li>Accelerators for agentic AI, large language models and multimodal foundation models</li><li>Computing-in-memory, near-memory and processing-in-sensor architectures</li><li>Emerging devices for AI: spintronic, resistive, ferroelectric, phase-change and photonic</li><li>Neuromorphic and spiking circuits and systems</li><li>Edge and on-device AI: low-power inference, on-chip learning and continual learning</li><li>Hardware–software co-design, compilers and AI for EDA</li><li>Chiplets, 3D integration and memory systems for AI</li><li>Trustworthy, secure and reliable AI hardware</li><li>AI circuits and systems for healthcare, mobility, manufacturing and smart cities</li></ul><h2>Paper Submission Guidelines</h2><p>The AICAS 2027 Organizing Committee invites interested authors to submit their previously unpublished research contributions from a broad range of topics related to Artificial Intelligence Circuits and Systems and its connections with other areas.</p><ul><li><strong><span style="color:blue">Important:</span></strong> The review process of regular papers will <strong>be double-blind</strong>. DO NOT reveal any authors' information (names, affiliations, email, grant information, personal acknowledgment, etc.) anywhere in the initial manuscript. You must also ensure that the metadata in the PDF does not include such information.</li><li>Full-length papers should have a maximum length of <strong>five (5) pages</strong> in PDF, with the fifth page reserved for <strong>references only</strong>.</li><li>The paper format should follow the <strong>IEEE conference templates for Letter page size</strong>.</li><li>Submitted manuscripts must describe <strong>original work</strong> which has not been submitted, accepted, or published in other conferences or journals.</li></ul><p>Please use the official IEEE conference templates in Letter page size to prepare your manuscript.</p><ul><li>Word Template: <a href="https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/conference-template-letter.docx">https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/conference-template-letter.docx</a></li><li>LaTeX Template: <a href="https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/conference-latex-template.zip">https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/conference-latex-template.zip</a></li></ul><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>March 10, 2027, Special session and tutorial proposals</li><li>April 13, 2027, Paper submission deadline</li><li>June 13, 2027, Notification of acceptance</li><li>July 23, 2027, Final paper and author registration</li></ul><h2>Publication</h2><p>Accepted and presented papers of AICAS 2027 will be submitted for inclusion in IEEE Xplore, subject to IEEE quality requirements.</p><h2>Call for Special Sessions</h2><p>The Organizing Committee of AICAS 2027 invites proposals for Special Sessions to be held during the conference.</p><p>Special sessions complement the main program by focusing on emerging topics or novel applications. Proposals should target timely, impactful research areas. While all Circuits and Systems topics are welcome, interdisciplinary research and the conference’s innovation themes are particularly encouraged:</p><ul><li>Hardware for embodied AI: perception, sensor fusion, motion control and robotics processors</li><li>Accelerators for agentic AI, large language models and multimodal foundation models</li><li>Computing-in-memory, near-memory and processing-in-sensor architectures</li><li>Emerging devices for AI: spintronic, resistive, ferroelectric, phase-change and photonic</li><li>Neuromorphic and spiking circuits and systems</li><li>Edge and on-device AI: low-power inference, on-chip learning and continual learning</li><li>Hardware–software co-design, compilers and AI for EDA</li><li>Chiplets, 3D integration and memory systems for AI</li><li>Trustworthy, secure and reliable AI hardware</li><li>AI circuits and systems for healthcare, mobility, manufacturing and smart cities</li></ul><h3>Proposal Requirements</h3><p>Proposals should include the following information (3 pages max.):</p><ol><li><strong>Title &amp; Abstract:</strong> A clear, concise title and abstract that outline the session’s core topic and scope.</li><li><strong>Rationale:</strong> Justify the topic’s novelty and timeliness, elaborate on its relevance to the CAS community, and demonstrate alignment with the conference’s innovation themes.</li><li><strong>Proposed Speakers:</strong> Submit a complete list of presentations and speakers (for each associated paper). Technical sessions typically require 5 papers. For special cases (e.g., invited industry speakers or extended talks), proposals for sessions with fewer papers are permitted.</li><li><strong>Short Biographies:</strong> Include brief bio-sketches of the session proposers.</li></ol><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Special session proposal deadline: March 10, 2027</li></ul><h3>Proposal Submission</h3><p>Special session proposals submission is to be announced. Please check back later for the submission link.</p><h2>Call for Tutorials</h2><p>The AICAS 2027 Organizing Committee invites proposals for tutorials to complement the regular program. Tutorials should provide in-depth coverage of emerging topics, offering a comprehensive overview and insights into the latest advancements for both researchers and practitioners.</p><h3>Tutorial Proposal Requirements</h3><p>Tutorial proposals to the AICAS 2027 should include:</p><ul><li>Title of the tutorial</li><li>Indicate short (1.5 hour) session or half-day (3 hours) session</li><li>Abstract</li><li>Names, affiliations, pictures, short bios, contact details, and expertise of presenters</li></ul><p>Note that important aspects in evaluating Tutorial proposals include the timeliness of the topic, quality/track record of the proposers, and expected value added to the overall technical program.</p><p>Join us in Hangzhou for AICAS 2027 and explore the intersection of cutting-edge AI and natural beauty!</p><h3>Tutorial Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Tutorial Proposal Submission Deadline: March 10, 2027</li><li>Tutorial Proposal Acceptance: May 31, 2027</li></ul><h3>Tutorial Proposal Submission</h3><p>Tutorial proposals submission is to be anounced soon. Please check back later for submission details.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email: aicas2027@youngac.cn</p><p>Phone: +86 132 8128 0917</p><p>Website: <a href="https://2027.ieee-aicas.org/">https://2027.ieee-aicas.org</a></p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
